# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# The reason is the same one that motivated putting this project under version
# control at all: several agents edit the same files from different shells
# (PowerShell, Git Bash) on Windows, and without this a single tool writing CRLF
# turns "what did the other agent change?" into a whole-file diff that answers
# nothing. `core.autocrlf` is a per-machine setting and cannot be relied on.
#
# Migration checksums hash exact raw bytes. Line-ending policy makes normal
# source diffs readable; it does not normalize checksum inputs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scanner parity fixtures deliberately retain CRLF bytes. Their exact physical
# lines prove COPY payload handling matches LF inputs.
/packages/architecture-tests/fixtures/migration-runner/999_cp1_runner_copy_payload_crlf_probe.sql -text
/packages/architecture-tests/fixtures/migration-runner/999_cp1_runner_copy_post_terminator_crlf_probe.sql -text

# Visual evidence and other binaries must never be line-ending filtered.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf binary
